The potential vulnerability is related to an Insecure Direct Object Reference (IDOR) vulnerability. This vulnerability arises because the application allows users to access or manipulate resources (such as products in the catalog) based on user-supplied identifiers (like product names) without proper authorization checks. If the application does not validate whether the user has permission to access or modify the specified resource, an attacker could exploit this by crafting requests to access or alter data that they should not have access to, leading to unauthorized data exposure or modification. This lack of access control can compromise the integrity and confidentiality of the product catalog.

